SHA-NI (Intel SHA Extensions) variant of sha256_block_data_order.

Source: BoringSSL gen/bcm/sha256-x86_64-linux.S
Repository: https://github.com/google/boringssl
License: dual OpenSSL License and SSLeay License (effectively BSD-style, MIT-compatible)

Only the sha256_block_data_order_hw function is vendored here; the other
variants (nohw / ssse3 / avx) in the upstream file are dropped because the
mbedtls path in signature_verify.cpp already covers CPUs without SHA-NI.
The #include <openssl/asm_base.h> is replaced with a minimal _CET_ENDBR
stub so this file builds without the rest of the BoringSSL tree.

